  "heat": 2,
  "text": "They found a lost scroll in the temple. The king had a building full of priests. He sent them to a woman. Second Kings twenty-two. They are renovating the temple, and Hilkiah the high priest finds the book of the law. Finds it. In the temple. That is its own scandal, and we are moving on. Shaphan the scribe reads it to King Josiah. And the king rends his clothes, because he can hear exactly how far the nation has drifted. So he needs a ruling. And he says, \"Go ye, enquire of the Lord for me, and for the people, and for all Judah, concerning the words of this book.\" Now think about who is standing in that room. A high priest. A scribe. A whole religious establishment on the payroll. And they go to Huldah the prophetess. Five men. Sent by a king. To a woman. For the authoritative reading of Scripture. And she does not soften it. She opens with, \"Thus saith the Lord God of Israel.\" Judgment on the nation. Then mercy for Josiah personally, because, she says, thine heart was tender. Her reading became national policy. The entire reformation that follows runs on what she said.",
